# SupportDesk – Customer Support Ticketing System
## Comprehensive Technical & Functional Project Documentation

---

## 1. Project Overview

**SupportDesk** is a modern, full-stack, enterprise-grade Customer Support Ticketing System designed to streamline technical support workflows, customer communication, issue tracking, and ticket lifecycle management. 

- **Project Name**: SupportDesk
- **Project Purpose**: Provide an isolated, secure, and intuitive web application for customers to lodge support tickets and track resolutions, while enabling support agents to claim, prioritize, manage, reply, and resolve issues effectively.
- **Application Capabilities**: Multi-role authentication (Customer & Support Agent), dynamic dashboard analytics, ticket creation with optional file attachments, automated Gemini AI classification recommendations, rich conversation threads with internal notes, full audit trail timeline logging, and multi-parameter searching/filtering.
- **Target Users**:
  1. **Customer**: End users seeking technical assistance, billing inquiries, account updates, or general support.
  2. **Support Agent**: Internal service specialists responsible for diagnosing issues, assigning tickets, communicating with customers, recording internal notes, and resolving support requests.
- **Main Objective**: Replace manual support channels (email, phone calls) with a centralized, transparent, and structured ticketing system that improves response times, enforces role authorization, and maintains a complete audit history.

> [!NOTE]
> **Role Scope Note**: The application strictly supports **Customer** and **Support Agent** user roles. There is no separate Admin Dashboard in the application scope.

