## 6. Main Features

### Customer Features
- **Registration**: Register account with Full Name, Email, Password, and Contact Number (`/register/customer`).
- **Authentication**: Secure Login (`/login`) with JWT token generation and session restoration on page reload.
- **Customer Dashboard**: Displays personal ticket metrics (Total, Open, In Progress, Resolved, Closed, Urgent).
- **Create Ticket**: Form supporting Title (min 5 chars), Description (min 10 chars), Category selection, Priority selection, optional File Attachment, and optional AI classification recommendations.
- **My Support Tickets**: Tabular list of customer-submitted tickets with status badges, priority badges, category badges, and assigned agent details.
- **Ticket Search & Advanced Filtering**: Search by Ticket Number, Title, or ID; filter by Status, Priority, Category, and Date Range (`From:` / `To:`).
- **Ticket Details View**: Displays issue details, timeline, ownership, conversation thread, attachment card, and audit history.
- **Conversation Thread**: Post replies to support agents. Replying to a `RESOLVED` or `CLOSED` ticket automatically reopens the ticket to `IN_PROGRESS`.
- **Ticket Closure**: Customers can confirm resolution and close resolved tickets.
- **File Attachments**: Upload file during ticket creation or upload/replace file later on existing tickets.
- **Attachment Replacement**: Uploading File B replaces File A as the current latest attachment while preserving File A metadata for audit history.
- **Activity History Log**: Chronological timeline displaying ticket creation, assignment, status changes, priority changes, comments, and attachment replacement events.
- **Logout**: Clears local storage tokens and invalidates user session.

### Support Agent Features
- **Authorized Registration**: Agent registration (`/register/agent`) requiring an authorized Agent ID (values `123` to `127`).
- **Support Agent Dashboard**: Global analytics panel tracking organization-wide ticket counts, open tickets, in-progress tickets, resolved tickets, and urgent issues.
- **Support Ticket Management Board**: Comprehensive board (`/agent/tickets`) listing all tickets across the organization.
- **Unassigned Filter**: Quick filter toggle to highlight unassigned customer tickets requiring ownership.
- **Advanced Multi-Filtering**: Search by Title/ID/Number, filter by Status, Priority, Category, Assigned Agent, and Date Range (`From:` / `To:`).
- **Ticket Ownership & Assignment**: Self-assign ticket ("Take Ownership") or reassign ticket to any registered support agent from a dropdown list. Auto-transitions `OPEN` tickets to `IN_PROGRESS` upon assignment.
- **Status Management**: Update ticket lifecycle status (`OPEN`, `IN_PROGRESS`, `RESOLVED`, `CLOSED`). Setting status to `RESOLVED` automatically sets `resolved_at` timestamp.
- **Priority Management**: Modify urgency/priority level (`LOW`, `MEDIUM`, `HIGH`, `URGENT`).
- **Customer Communication**: Post public replies visible to the customer.
- **Internal Notes**: Create private internal notes (marked with a lock icon) visible exclusively to support agents. Internal notes are completely isolated from customers at the SQL query layer.
- **Attachment Viewing & Download**: Inspect customer attachments, view file metadata (size, upload date, uploader), and download latest attached files.
- **Activity Log Inspection**: View real-time audit history of all actions performed on a ticket.

